From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:08:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot: Start services.exe in session 0.

Since Windows Vista services run in session 0, apart from the user's session, and programs rely on
it: .NET's IsWindowsService(), of Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.WindowsServices, tells a service from
a program by its parent being services.exe in session 0, and a .NET service that finds otherwise
runs as a console program and never answers the service manager, which then fails it with
ERROR_SERVICE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT.  OfficePLUS's service, for one.

services.exe gets the token of SYSTEM, which it stands in for, as far as that goes here: in session 0,
and with SeTcbPrivilege enabled, which its services inherit to start programs in the user's session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/tests/process.c b/dlls/kernel32/tests/process.c
